  "summary": "Cart Behaviour – Price Recalculation",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18557",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n**I want** the cart to automatically display Was/Now pricing when a sale is active and return to the full RRP when it ends, \n**so that** I always see the correct price without needing to manually refresh.\n\nWhen a product in the cart moves onto a sale price — whether via the SFCC sale pricebook ([SFCC-37](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-37)) or the SFCC Promotion Engine — the cart must show the Was/Now price treatment on that line item automatically on next cart load. \nWhen the sale or promotion ends, the Was/Now treatment must disappear and the full RRP must be restored. No action from the Shopper is required.\n\nNo notification, alert, or banner is shown when prices change, the update is silent.\n\nSFCC basket recalculation is OOTB behavior — confirmed by dev as automatic on every basket retrieval. This story covers the Was/Now display output of that recalculation specifically on the cart page. Was/Now visual design is owned by [SFCC-464](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-464).\n\n\nReference Image (Figma is leading)\n\n![\"image-20260804-020500.png\"](image-20260804-020500.png)",
